# ===== 5. SOLUTION OVERVIEW =====
rep('<h2 class="section-title">TITAN — one system, five integrated domains.</h2>',
    '<h2 class="section-title">TITAN — five integrated domains, one source of truth.</h2>', 'solution title')

rep('<p class="section-lead">TITAN is not a wrapper around MCTFS. It replaces MCTFS as the authoritative pay and personnel system and consolidates the fragmented ecosystem into five integrated domains sharing a single data model and a single Marine record. The one constraint that cannot be removed: the Defense Joint Military Pay System (DCPS) is DoD-level infrastructure — TITAN interfaces with DCPS, it does not replace it.</p>',
    '<p class="section-lead">TITAN is not a MCTFS replacement. The root problem is not that MCTFS is wrong — it is that nothing connects back to it. TITAN is the connective tissue: a Talent Intelligence platform that reads from MCTFS, integrates the downstream systems that should be feeding it, and surfaces a unified picture to every user who needs it. Talent management is a <em>capability</em> this platform enables. Five integrated domains share one data model and one access layer, turning isolated data into institutional decision advantage.</p>', 'solution overview lead')

rep('''    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #C8A951">
      <div class="card-title">Governing Architecture Principle</div>
      <div class="card-body">Every domain reads from and writes to a single data model. There is no extract-transform-load between domains. A reenlistment action in Domain 4 immediately updates the Marine's record in Domain 1, the billet fill status in Domain 2, the retention inventory in Domain 3, and the readiness dashboard in Domain 5 — simultaneously, without human intervention.</div>
    </div>''',
    '''    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #C8A951">
      <div class="card-title">Governing Architecture Principle</div>
      <div class="card-body">Every domain reads from a single data model anchored to MCTFS. Policy documents — DoD directives, SecNavInsts, MCOs, MARADMINs — are ingested and semantically indexed, surfacing policy context at the point of every decision. A reenlistment action updates the Marine's record, billet fill status, retention inventory, and readiness dashboard simultaneously — no ETL lag, no manual reconciliation.</div>
    </div>''', 'governing architecture card')

rep('''    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #C8A951">
      <div class="card-title">MCTFS Transition</div>
